Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?O0:=20CI=20baseline=20=E2=80=94=20the=20checked?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20shard=20registry=20(target=20registry=20check).?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The CI layout is a checked registry (D-O0-1): ci/registry.txt pins the ten
lanes of CONTRIBUTING.md (core, state, exec, consensus, net, node, wallet,
ecosystem, security, perf) over the workspace's --lib and tests/* targets
(127 today), each lane pinning its main test (a shard that does not run its
main test is a dead gate). aura-ci check (the target registry check, D-O0-2)
validates the registry against the discovered tree and the workflow matrix
and runs inside make test: a disabled shard holding targets is
'error: ci: shard security disabled' -> exit 65 -> CI red.

Named control: disabled_shard_refused (exit 65, error: ci: shard security
disabled); 6/6 mutation NC red (tools/nc_o0.py); 10/10 golden scenarios
+ count guard (independent Python oracle tools/gen_o0_vectors.py ->
tests/o0_ci.rs). make ci-sync re-registers targets by the documented lane
table (phase prefix -> lane) preserving disabled flags and canonical main
pins; aura-ci run --shard <lane> emits only plain cargo test commands from
the registry (D-O0-3, no secret shards); make coverage writes the
deterministic target-coverage report (docs/coverage.txt: 127/127, 100.0%).

Workflow: the H7 least-privilege baseline is untouched; O0 adds the
registry job (make ci-check), the ten-lane test matrix (make ci-shard
SHARD=<lane>) and the coverage job, each with cargo cache on Cargo.lock.
